    {
      "id": "im-02-irregular",
      "title": "Step 2: Irregular commands: sois, aie, sache, va",
      "fr": "l'impératif irrégulier",
      "level": "A1",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "imperative",
        "irregular",
        "sois",
        "soyez",
        "aie",
        "ayez",
        "sache",
        "veuillez",
        "va",
        "fais",
        "dites"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "imperative"
      ],
      "tense": "imperatif-present",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Only a few verbs are irregular in commands, but they are very common. **Être, avoir, savoir, vouloir** take their forms from the subjunctive, **aller** is *va*, and **faire, dire** have *faites, dites*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "verb",
                "tu",
                "nous",
                "vous"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "être",
                  "sois",
                  "soyons",
                  "soyez"
                ],
                [
                  "avoir",
                  "aie",
                  "ayons",
                  "ayez"
                ],
                [
                  "savoir",
                  "sache",
                  "sachons",
                  "sachez"
                ],
                [
                  "vouloir",
                  "veuille",
                  "veuillons",
                  "veuillez"
                ],
                [
                  "aller",
                  "va",
                  "allons",
                  "allez"
                ],
                [
                  "faire",
                  "fais",
                  "faisons",
                  "faites"
                ],
                [
                  "dire",
                  "dis",
                  "disons",
                  "dites"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Être and avoir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Sois sage !* (Be good!) *Soyez à l'heure !* (Be on time!) *N'aie pas peur !* (Don't be afraid!) *Ayez confiance !* (Have confidence!)"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "___ gentil avec ta sœur !",
                "a": [
                  "Sois"
                ],
                "hint": "être",
                "en": "Be nice to your sister!"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Savoir and vouloir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Sachez que...* (Please note that...) is formal. *Veuillez* + infinitive is a very polite request, used in letters, emails and announcements: *Veuillez patienter.* (Please wait.)"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "Please wait. (announcement)",
                "a": [
                  "Veuillez patienter."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Faire, dire, aller",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Fais attention !* (Be careful!) *Faites vite !* (Be quick!) *Dites bonjour !* (Say hello!) *Va au lit !* (Go to bed!)"
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "___ attention, la route est glissante !",
                "a": [
                  "Fais",
                  "Faites"
                ],
                "hint": "faire",
                "en": "Be careful, the road is slippery!"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Watch out",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "*Aie* has no -s and sounds like *et*: *N'aie pas peur.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "*Faites* and *dites* are the same as in the present: *vous faites, vous dites*. Not *faisez* or *disez*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Sois prudent sur ton vélo !",
                  "en": "Be careful on your bike!"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "N'ayez pas peur, le chien est gentil.",
                  "en": "Don't be afraid, the dog is friendly."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Va chercher ton frère !",
                  "en": "Go and get your brother!"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Dites-moi la vérité !",
                  "en": "Tell me the truth!"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Veuillez fermer la porte.",
                  "en": "Please close the door."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
