    {
      "id": "im-06-polite-mix",
      "title": "Step 6: Polite requests and mixed practice",
      "fr": "demander poliment",
      "level": "A2",
      "keywords": [
        "step by step",
        "imperative",
        "polite",
        "s'il vous plaît",
        "pourriez-vous",
        "infinitive instructions",
        "mix"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "imperative",
        "conditionnel"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "A bare command can sound rude to an adult. Soften it with **s'il te plaît / s'il vous plaît**, or ask a question instead: *Tu peux fermer la fenêtre ? Pourriez-vous m'aider ?* Instructions and signs often use the **infinitive**: *Ne pas fumer. Mélanger la farine et les œufs.*"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Softer ways to ask",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "command",
                "softer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Ferme la fenêtre !",
                  "Tu peux fermer la fenêtre, s'il te plaît ?"
                ],
                [
                  "Aidez-moi !",
                  "Pourriez-vous m'aider ?"
                ],
                [
                  "Donne-moi le sel.",
                  "Tu me passes le sel ?"
                ],
                [
                  "Attendez.",
                  "Veuillez patienter."
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "Could you help me? (polite)",
                "a": [
                  "Pourriez-vous m'aider ?",
                  "Pouvez-vous m'aider ?",
                  "Vous pourriez m'aider ?",
                  "Vous pouvez m'aider ?"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Instructions with the infinitive",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Recipes, exam tasks and signs use the infinitive instead of a command: *Lire le texte et répondre aux questions. Ne pas toucher.* The negative puts **ne pas together before** the infinitive."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "Do not smoke. (a sign)",
                "a": [
                  "Ne pas fumer."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Passe-moi le pain, s'il te plaît.",
                  "en": "Pass me the bread, please."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Pourriez-vous parler plus lentement ?",
                  "en": "Could you speak more slowly?"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Ne pas marcher sur la pelouse.",
                  "en": "Do not walk on the grass."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Couper les tomates en morceaux.",
                  "en": "Cut the tomatoes into pieces."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
